From 5e10f4611f17d18ecc8d26fa07d1350a29bf61b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "osman.yagci" <osmnyagc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:04:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mesa: don't advertise APIs that are not built

_mesa_get_version() returns a version for every API, whether or not it
was built in. With -Dgles1=disabled it still returns 11 for
API_OPENGLES, so the DRI frontend sets __DRI_API_GLES in the screen's
api_mask and EGL puts EGL_OPENGL_ES_BIT in every config's
EGL_RENDERABLE_TYPE and EGL_CONFORMANT. Creating that context then fails
in _mesa_initialize_context(), which refuses an API that is not built,
and the failure reaches the application as EGL_BAD_ALLOC.

dEQP-EGL trusts the config: create_context.* fail with "Failed to create
context", create_context.no_config fails because it accepts only
EGL_BAD_MATCH for an unsupported GLES1, and every surfaceless_context.*
case ends with a fatal ResourceError that terminates the session.

-Dopengl=false and -Dgles2=disabled have the same problem. Compile out
the cases of the APIs that are not built, so they fall through to the
trailing return 0. The api_mask then carries no bit for them, no config
advertises them, and a GLES1 request without a config fails with
__DRI_CTX_ERROR_BAD_VERSION, i.e. EGL_BAD_MATCH. The default label keeps
-Wswitch quiet when a case is compiled out.

Fixes: 8bb1ecaa021 ("mesa/main: Exit early when trying to create an unsupported context API")
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46169>
(cherry picked from commit 338afb32f868e8607e7f082381dc859dae5583e8)
Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/5e10f4611f17d18ecc8d26fa07d1350a29bf61b9
[ adapted: dropped .pick_status.json, not in the 26.3.0 tarball or bookkeeping only ]
---
 .pick_status.json       | 2 +-
 src/mesa/main/version.c | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/version.c b/src/mesa/main/version.c
index ec4848f7173e..2747083f1baa 100644
--- a/src/mesa/main/version.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/version.c
@@ -573,6 +573,7 @@ _mesa_get_version(const struct gl_extensions *extensions,
                   struct gl_constants *consts, gl_api api)
 {
    switch (api) {
+#if HAVE_OPENGL
    case API_OPENGL_COMPAT:
       /* Disable higher GLSL versions for legacy contexts.
        * This disallows creation of higher compatibility contexts. */
@@ -582,10 +583,17 @@ _mesa_get_version(const struct gl_extensions *extensions,
       FALLTHROUGH;
    case API_OPENGL_CORE:
       return compute_version(extensions, consts, api);
+#endif
+#if HAVE_OPENGL_ES_1
    case API_OPENGLES:
       return 11;
+#endif
+#if HAVE_OPENGL_ES_2
    case API_OPENGLES2:
       return compute_version_es2(extensions, consts);
+#endif
+   default:
+      break;
    }
    return 0;
 }
